# RiteMark Patch: browser-context-bridge
#
# Purpose: Expose active integrated-browser metadata, page summary, screenshot,
#          and auto-share trigger to the Ritemark extension host via workbench
#          commands, enabling browser-aware AI chat context (Sprint 67); and
#          push each top-level navigation and title change to the extension
#          for the Browser Recent list (Sprint 131, #195).
#
# Why:
#   The Ritemark AI sidebar (Claude Code SDK, Codex) needs to answer
#   questions about the page the user is looking at in the integrated
#   browser. The extension host cannot reach workbench services directly
#   (IBrowserViewWorkbenchService, IPlaywrightService), so we expose a
#   small, focused bridge as six Action2 commands:
#
#     workbench.action.browser.getActiveContext              - URL/title/focus/state
#     workbench.action.browser.getActiveSummary              - bounded page summary
#     workbench.action.browser.captureActiveViewport         - JPEG viewport screenshot
#     workbench.action.browser.toggleAnnotationMode          - toolbar toggle (screenshot)
#     workbench.action.browser.getAnnotationMode             - read annotation flag
#     workbench.action.browser.ensureActiveBrowserShared     - trigger share consent prompt
#
#   Annotation mode is a separate workbench-owned per-tab state distinct
#   from `sharedWithAgent`. Sharing alone enables URL/title + bounded
#   summary; annotation mode additionally permits the per-turn viewport
#   screenshot. This keeps the per-turn token/screenshot cost opt-in
#   (Sprint 67 D5 + D8).
#
#   Auto-share command lets the extension request "Share with Agent?"
#   consent automatically when a new browser tab becomes the active
#   context (Sprint 67 D8 addendum). The workbench respects the existing
#   "Don't ask again" preference, so after first consent the prompt
#   stops appearing.
#
#   The toolbar action lives in MenuId.BrowserActionsToolbar near
#   DevTools so the toggle sits in the same place users already access
#   browser-level actions.
#
#   Navigation push (Sprint 131): RitemarkBrowserHistoryContribution follows
#   the browser tab each editor pane shows and calls the extension command
#   `ritemark.browser.didNavigate` with { kind, pageId, url, title, failed,
#   ephemeral } on every onDidNavigate / onDidChangeTitle, and once when a
#   tab is first shown (a background tab loads while no pane listens). It is
#   the bridge's only workbench -> extension push. The extension owns every
#   filtering rule (extensions/ritemark/src/browser/browserNavigationRecorder.ts);
#   a missing listener is dropped with a trace log, never an error.
#
# File(s):
#   src/vs/platform/browserView/common/browserView.ts
#   src/vs/workbench/contrib/browserView/common/browserView.ts
#   src/vs/workbench/contrib/browserView/electron-browser/browserView.contribution.ts
#   src/vs/workbench/contrib/browserView/electron-browser/features/ritemarkBrowserContextFeature.ts
#
#   The share question (Sprint 134, R20, #455): upstream's modal "Share with
#   Agent?" dialog blocked the window. ensureActiveBrowserShared now opens no
#   dialog: with no argument it shares only when the person chose to share
#   pages without asking (the model's ritemarkSharesWithoutAsking), else it
#   returns needsAnswer and the extension asks on the AI's sheet. With the
#   sheet's answer { pageId, answer: 'share' | 'notNow', withoutAsking } it
#   shares through the model's shareWithAgentAnswered (what Allow does: the
#   network policy's notice first, the stored choice only with the box), and
#   an answer about a page no longer in front is stale and shares nothing.
#   Annotation mode, control consent and upstream's toggle keep the dialog.
#
#   The site's icon (Sprint 134, R18): the navigation push also reports the
#   tab's favicon changes (kind 'favicon', the model's data URL), so Recent's
#   rows show the site's icon.
#
# Created: 2026-05-11
# Updated: 2026-10-12 (Sprint 131: navigation push for Browser Recent)
# Updated: 2026-10-19 (Sprint 134: the share question on the AI's sheet)
#
